## Common commands

On Windows use `flow` (or `flow.cmd`) instead of `./flow`.

```sh
./flow list --all          # commands, aliases, run steps and matrix keys
./flow config --dbg        # {{#with.conan}}Conan install + {{/with.conan}}{{#with.cmake}}CMake {{/with.cmake}}configure, Debug
./flow build --dbg         # build Debug
./flow test --dbg          # build and run tests, Debug
./flow test --both         # same, for Debug and Release
./flow test --sane         # Debug with sanitizers
./flow verify --rel        # build, test, sign, pack and install-check, Release
./flow run -s Build,Test -D build_type=Debug compiler=clang
./flow run --dry-run --dbg # print what would run, do nothing
```

- `config`, `build`, `test` and `verify` are aliases defined in `entry` of `.flow/config.yml`; each runs a fixed list of steps.
- `-D key=value` filters the build matrix in `.flow/matrix.yml` (keys: `compiler`, `build_type`, `sanitizer`, `os`). `--dbg`, `--rel`, `--both` and `--sane` are shortcuts for common `-D` sets.
- `-E w-error=on` turns warnings into errors.
- `--official` limits the matrix to the release builds listed in `.flow/official.yml`.

Build trees go to `build/debug` and `build/release`. Test reports (JUnit XML) are written under `build/<config>/test-results/`.

## Layout

- `.flow/`
  - `flow.py` bootstraps the project: pins proj-flow to {{__flow_version__}} and installs it into `.venv/`
  - `config.yml` lists extensions, run aliases (`entry`), compiler names{{#with.cmake}}, CMake variables{{/with.cmake}} and shortcuts
  - `matrix.yml` is the build matrix: compiler x build_type x sanitizer x os
  - `official.yml` filters the matrix down to release builds (`--official`)
{{#with.cmake}}
  - `cmake/` holds CMake modules; `common.cmake` has `add_project_test()` and `add_win32_icon()`
  - `packages/` holds the CPack setup (TGZ/DEB on Linux, ZIP/WiX on Windows)
  - `extensions/{{FLOW_PACKAGE}}/` holds project-local proj-flow extensions (Python), e.g. the Icons step
{{/with.cmake}}
- `flow`, `flow.cmd` are wrappers calling `.flow/flow.py`
{{#with.cmake}}
- `CMakeLists.txt` is the top-level project; its options use the `{{NAME_PREFIX}}_` prefix
- `CMakePresets.json` has debug/release presets, with Ninja, Makefile and Visual Studio variants
{{/with.cmake}}
{{#with.conan}}
- `conanfile.txt` lists Conan requirements
{{/with.conan}}
{{#with.libs}}
- `libs/`, with `CMakeLists.txt` adding the subdirectories below
  - `{{LIB_NAME}}/`
    - `{{INCLUDEDIR}}/` public headers
    - `{{SRCDIR}}/` sources, private headers and `version{{EXT.hxx}}.in`
    - `tests/` GoogleTest sources, listed in `TEST_SRCS` of `{{LIB_NAME}}-test`
{{#cmake.application}}
  - `app/{{SRCDIR}}/main{{EXT.cxx}}` is the entry point, linking `{{LIB_NAME}}`
{{/cmake.application}}
{{/with.libs}}
{{^with.libs}}
{{#with.cmake}}
